            <div xml:id="d790">

                <pb facs="0741" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1997: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-01T19:00:00-05:00">March 1, 1940—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Your 92, February 24, 11 a.m., and Shanghai’s 159, February 26, 2 p.m.,
                    Shanghai extra-Settlement roads. You are authorized <pb facs="0742" n="734"
                        xml:id="pg734"/> to reply to the Chinese Foreign Office along the lines of
                    the draft outlined in your telegram under reference, amended as suggested in
                    Shanghai’s 159, February 26, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
